---
import ImplementationSupport from './ImplementationSupport.astro';
import DocumentationLayout from '../../layouts/DocumentationLayout.astro';
import PreviewControls from './PreviewControls.astro';
import MerchantListingPreview from './MerchantListingPreview.astro';
import {CodeSnippet} from '../dmf-ui/code-block';
import {blocks} from '../../data/blocks';
import catalog from '../../../contracts/catalog.json';
const block=blocks.find(b=>b.slug==='merchant-listing')!,record=catalog.blocks.find(b=>b.slug==='merchant-listing')!,react=catalog.react.blocks.find(b=>b.name==='MerchantListingBlock')!;
---
<DocumentationLayout title="MerchantListingBlock" description={block.description} section="blocks" crumbs={[{name:'Blocks',href:'/blocks/'},{name:'MerchantListingBlock'}]} toc={[{id:'preview',title:'Live preview'},{id:'usage',title:'Usage'},{id:'api',title:'API and states'},{id:'behavior',title:'Behavior and accessibility'},{id:'limits',title:'Limits'}]}>
 <h1 class="docs-block-title">MerchantListingBlock</h1><p class="docs-lead">{block.description}</p><ImplementationSupport slug={'merchant-listing'} kind="block"/>
 <section id="preview" class="docs-section"><h2>Live preview</h2><PreviewControls/><MerchantListingPreview/></section>
 <section id="usage" class="docs-section"><h2>Usage</h2><p>Import shared styles once and use a .dmf-ui scope. Author semantic item content with real destinations. The sample below is explicitly illustrative and adds no data service.</p><CodeSnippet code={block.usage} language="astro" title="Astro item function slot" wrap/><CodeSnippet code={`import {MerchantListingBlock} from '@dmf-ui/react';\nimport '@dmf-ui/react/styles.css';\n\nconst items=[{id:'sample',name:'Sample merchant',href:'#sample-details'}];\n<MerchantListingBlock id="merchants" title="Sample merchants" items={items}\n  getItemKey={item=>item.id}\n  renderItem={item=><h3><a href={item.href}>{item.name}</a></h3>}\n/>\n// The host must also render the sample-details destination.`} language="tsx" title="React generic item rendering" wrap/></section>
 <section id="api" class="docs-section docs-prose"><h2>API and states</h2><p>Required: id, title, items and getItemKey. React also requires renderItem; Astro requires an item function slot when ready items are populated. React infers the item type from items. Astro exposes unknown item data at its key callback, so narrow or cast data owned by your application. No universal merchant schema is imposed.</p><p>Keys must be unique nonempty strings, derived from stable identity rather than positions. React uses them as list keys. Astro validates identity while rendering static HTML; no client reconciliation is implied. A ready empty array renders the empty view. Loading/error hide stale items and pagination; neither calls the item renderer. getItemKey/renderItem must be pure.</p><p>status defaults to ready (ready/loading/error). headingLevel defaults to h2 (h1/h2/h3). Description, loading/empty/error copy and statusMessage are configurable. React has actions, pagination, emptyContent, errorContent, loadingContent and children; Astro has corresponding actions/pagination/empty/error/loading/default slots. Custom error content is wrapped in an alert. Hosts own retry actions and focus. The library adds no fake retry button.</p><CodeSnippet code={record.declaration} language="ts" title="Astro Props" wrap/><CodeSnippet code={react.types[0].declaration} language="ts" title="React Props" wrap/><div class="docs-table-scroll"><table class="docs-options"><thead><tr><th>Property</th><th>Astro default</th></tr></thead><tbody>{Object.entries(record.defaults).map(([key,value])=><tr><td><code>{key}</code></td><td><code>{String(value)}</code></td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div></section>
 <section id="behavior" class="docs-section docs-prose"><h2>Behavior and accessibility</h2><p>The labelled section contains a native list and one list item per authored result. Cards and their headings, alternatives, links and optional controls are host compositions. Avoid nested interactive card targets and duplicated ids. Use the existing MerchantCard component or supply a different card composition; no RatingDisplay alias is added.</p><p>The result container is busy only during loading. A separate polite status region sits outside that busy container, using loadingLabel by default while loading. Hosts supply statusMessage for result updates; counts are not invented or announced automatically. Static placeholders are decorative, unanimated and unfocusable. Empty is a result view, not an error alert. Test custom content independently.</p><p>The grid follows section-container width: one column by default, two at 36rem and three at 60rem. Narrow containers stack even on desktop. Logical spacing, wrapping, shrinkable tracks and natural control sizing support standard RTL and separately enlarged text. Focus outlines remain visible in forced colors. Brand appearance remains independent of data and layout.</p></section>
 <section id="limits" class="docs-section docs-prose"><h2>Dependencies and limits</h2><p>Astro reuses Text, EmptyState and Skeleton. React reuses Text and existing skeleton styling. The examples compose Card, Image and Badge; those are host choices, not mandatory item dependencies. {block.limitations}</p><p>DMF light/dark and HUI light form the scoped browser matrix. White HUI/CB primary labels retain their documented contrast exceptions. Source/DOM checks do not establish spoken announcements or physical-device acceptance. Safari/Firefox and spoken-reader acceptance for this Block remain unverified.</p><p>Sources: <code>{record.source}</code> and <code>{react.source}</code>. <a href="/docs/architecture/">Architecture and responsive conventions</a>.</p></section>
</DocumentationLayout>
